CC   Original source text: Human spleen genomic DNA.
CC   This pseudogene occurs on a chromosome different from the normal
CC   lambda genes, which are on chromosome 22. The authors [1] believe
CC   that this pseudogene might be a result of processing by an RNA
CC   intermediate, because the intervening sequences are spliced out and
CC   the 3' end contains a poly-A-like sequence. [1] also sequenced the
CC   homologous active C-lambda gene Ke- Oz+ (C3).
